  nonce: 96f7  # 96f7
  message: "Clause (a1) progress, not closure. PR #207 removed one source of unrealizable/missed sink attribution: the module hint handed to _lookup_named_entry was truncated at the first colon, which for rust meant all nine of its catalogued sink modules (std::fs, std::process, std::io, ...) could never match, so a correctly-identified sink was rejected while an unidentified one matched. Measured effect on the 9-repo cohort is +1 flow (a real std::env.var_os source) and 0 lost - small today because rust analyzers emit the `external` sentinel for 396 of 449 unresolved taint call edges. The item stays violated: (a1) is not closed by one matching fix, (a2) is still vacuously true while section 3a is confirm-only, (b) carries three filed limits, and (a3)/(c) are met. Do NOT close on this."  # 96f7
- op: discuss  # f0d6
  at: '2026-08-05T08:14:22Z'  # f0d6
  by: agent  # f0d6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f0d6
  clock: 27  # f0d6
  nonce: f0d6  # f0d6
  message: "CLAUSE (b) SCOPE PUBLISHED, CLAUSE NOT CLOSED, ITEM STAYS VIOLATED. PR #214, dev 66798299bc.\nClause (b) is sanitizer neutralization. Two things moved and neither closes it.\n1. THE MECHANISM IS LESS WRONG. A sanitizer called in the SAME function as the source was ignored\n   outright -- the BFS barrier exempts the seed (it must; the seed is the taint origin and has to\n   stay reachable) and that exemption also means a barrier called FROM the seed function is never\n   consulted. Encrypt-then-write in one function is an ordinary shape, so every such site reported\n   a false violation. Now honoured on the DDG pass, on positive evidence only: two walks must\n   agree, unrestricted confirming a data route and a barrier-respecting walk exhausting every\n   route with each step accounted for. See WI-fasub for the repro table and the four mutation\n   tests. The structural pass cannot honour it at all, permanently -- a call graph records no\n   order between two calls sharing a caller -- and that is now published rather than folklore.\n2. THE SCOPE IS PUBLISHED, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES (b) EVIDENCE READABLE AT ALL. The sanitizer\n   catalogue is 12 entries across 5 languages and EVERY ONE IS CRYPTOGRAPHIC (plaintext ->\n   ciphertext, key_material -> derived_key). So a repository-wide 0 sanitized flows carries the\n   L58 ambiguity: nothing was protected, or nothing COULD be, because the claim taint labels and\n   the sanitizer input labels are disjoint sets. MEASURED on the nine-repo cohort with production\n   own registrar and it is the second reading: 0 sanitizer call sites across 95,950 taint call\n   edges, positive control firing, and exactly ONE pre-gate name hit cohort-wide which the\n   INV-finoh gate refuses correctly. New sanitizer_scope block nested in dataflow_coverage\n   (envelope schema 1.7 -> 1.8, additive, on BOTH surfaces): catalogue size, languages carrying\n   entries, the input-to-output categories it can express, sanitizable_labels, and\n   same_function_honoured_by. Categories and labels are DERIVED from the loaded catalogue, so\n   extending it moves the disclosure without an edit.\nWHY (b) IS NOT MET. A disclosure is not a verification. Clause (b) was measured in August and\nHOLDS -- for one taint-category family, which is the only family the catalogue can express. For\nevery other taint label in the source catalogue there is no sanitizer entry, so the clause is\nUNMEASURABLE rather than satisfied, and reporting the crypto result unqualified would be exactly\nthe unscoped overstatement L23 governs. What would close it is a sanitizer vocabulary beyond\ncrypto, not more work on the propagators.\nCLAUSE LEDGER, UNCHANGED OTHERWISE, AND DO NOT CLOSE THIS ITEM ON ANY ONE OF THEM (L14 -- its own\nhistory has been corrected for that twice): (a1) attribution soundness ADVANCED by the matching\nfixes and not closed; (a2) data-flow consistency VACUOUSLY TRUE while section 3a is confirm-only,\nwhich is machine-readable as inclusion_decided_by = call_graph_reachability; (a3) published scope\nMET at PR #204; (b) mechanism improved and scope published, family limit stands; (c) honest\nlabelling MET."  # f0d6
- op: discuss  # e5a9
  at: '2026-08-06T17:21:08Z'  # e5a9
  by: agent  # e5a9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e5a9
  clock: 28  # e5a9
  nonce: e5a9  # e5a9
  message: "CLAUSE (b) CORROBORATED FROM THE OTHER END OF THE PIPELINE, 2026-08-06, and the\nconsequence is larger than the clause. Clause (b) measured \"0 registered\nsanitizer call sites across 95,950 taint call edges\" at the EDGE INDEX on one\nrepo. Measured instead at the WALK, on four repos, by reading the arm directly\noff barrier_lines:\n\n    repo          walk invocations   3a arm   BARRIER arm\n    hypergumbo          36             36          0\n    pretix              35             35          0\n    prometheus           7              7          0\n    alertmanager         3              3          0\n\nZERO barrier-arm walks anywhere. Two independent instruments, two different\nlayers, same answer: the sanitizer half of the pipeline has no live traffic.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND THIS CLAUSE. The barrier arm is the ONLY consumer of a\nFalse verdict from the section 3a walk -- the 3a arm tests \"is True\", so False\nand None collapse there. So with zero barrier walks:\n\n  * the WI-joluk coverage gate cannot fire (it blocks False only);\n  * every proposal to reclassify escape sites (expression reads, section 7a\n    field sensitivity) is structurally inert -- it can neither delete nor add\n    a finding;\n  * the suppression hazard that has governed this whole area since PR #214 --\n    \"a False earns sanitized, so removing blockers deletes findings\" -- is REAL\n    but NOT YET LIVE.\n\nThat last point reverses an ordering intuition worth recording explicitly: a\nsanitizer catalogue is what ARMS the removal hazard. Catalogue work does not\nrelieve the danger, it creates it. Anything that grows the sanitizer vocabulary\nshould land AFTER, not before, the gates that protect the False path -- which is\nthe order WI-joluk already argued for and has now been given a second reason.\n\nNOT MEASURED HERE: whether the crypto-only vocabulary is the whole cause. The\nbarrier arm also requires 3a to have returned True first, and only 32 of the\n81 walks across this cohort did (hypergumbo 21, pretix 8, prometheus 2,\nalertmanager 1). So even a rich sanitizer catalogue would only reach flows that\n3a already confirms. Both conditions are conjunctive and only one has been\nattributed."  # e5a9
- op: discuss  # 8f31
  at: '2026-08-06T18:30:17Z'  # 8f31
  by: agent  # 8f31
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8f31
  clock: 29  # 8f31
  nonce: 8f31  # 8f31
  message: "CORRECTION to my note above, same day. I reported the zero barrier-arm\nwalk count as corroborating clause (b) 'from the other end of the\npipeline'. It does not corroborate it -- it is confounded with a\ndifferent defect, and I did not exclude that before filing.\n\nWHAT I CLAIMED, HOURS EARLIER TODAY: zero barrier-arm walks BECAUSE the\nshipped sanitizer vocabulary is crypto-only -- and therefore \"a sanitizer\ncatalogue ARMS the removal hazard; catalogue growth creates the danger, so\ngates land before catalogue growth.\"\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT ESTABLISHED: I never positive-controlled the zero. A null\nbelieved without demonstrating the instrument can produce a known positive is\nthe exact rule this repo has written down, and I violated it the same day I\nedited it into LIVE.md. It is also the shape of this area's own invalidated\n0.00% confident-negative figure: a tautology of the configuration.\n\nTWO PURPOSE-BUILT FIXTURES, BOTH ZERO WALKS:\n  v1  f = Fernet(key); plain = f.decrypt(tok); cipher = f.encrypt(plain);\n      pathlib.Path(...).write_text(cipher)\n      -> the crypto calls emit python:external:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol.\n         The receiver type is never inferred, so the SOURCE cannot match\n         cryptography.fernet.Fernet.decrypt and the SANITIZER cannot match\n         Fernet.encrypt. No flow exists for a barrier to guard.\n  v2  the same shape written MODULE-QUALIFIED, removing receiver typing as a\n      variable -> source and sanitizer now resolve\n      (python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol), but the\n      SINK emits NO call edge at all: pathlib.Path(...).write_text(x) is an\n      attribute chain rooted at a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT. Still zero walks.\n\nSO THE BARRIER ARM IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE SAME ROOT CAUSE AS THE REST OF THIS\nAREA. Every sanitizer in the shipped catalogue is an INSTANCE METHOD --\nFernet.encrypt, AESGCM.encrypt, AEAD.Seal, Cipher.doFinal -- and\ninstance-method receiver typing is precisely what is broken (INV-linub). That\nis a THIRD symptom family from one root cause, alongside io-boundary catalogue\nreach and the section 4 summary lookup inside the walk.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: the observation (0 barrier walks across 4 repos and 2 fixtures)\nand the practical verdict (an escape reclassification cannot move a finding\ntoday). WHAT DOES NOT: the mechanism, and every sequencing conclusion built on\nit. Catalogue growth CANNOT arm the hazard while receiver typing is broken.\nRECEIVER TYPING IS WHAT ARMS IT.\n\nSTILL OPEN, stated rather than papered over: I could not construct a barrier\nwalk in ANY configuration, so I cannot distinguish \"reachable, and nothing in\nthe corpus hits it\" from \"effectively dead on the DDG path\". There is also NO\nend-to-end test driving the barrier arm through propagate_taint_ddg -- the one\n'sanitized' test uses propagate_taint_structural. A positive control is a\nprerequisite for any future claim about this arm, mine included.\n\nSO THE TWO ZEROS ARE NOT INDEPENDENT MEASUREMENTS OF THE SAME FACT.\nClause (b) counted registered sanitizer CALL SITES; my probe counted\nbarrier WALKS. Both are zero, but a sanitizer call site can only register\nif the sanitizer's callee resolves -- and every shipped sanitizer is an\ninstance method whose receiver type is not inferred. So clause (b)'s own\nzero may ALSO be an INV-linub artifact rather than a statement about the\nvocabulary. Two instruments agreeing while sharing an upstream defect is\nagreement about the defect, not about the world.\n\nWHAT CLAUSE (b) SHOULD BE RE-MEASURED WITH, once receiver typing lands:\na positive control demonstrating a sanitizer CAN register at all, then\nthe count. Until then the clause's zero should not be cited as evidence\nthat the sanitizer vocabulary is too narrow -- that conclusion is not\nyet separable from the receiver-typing gap."  # 8f31
- op: discuss  # ede3
  at: '2026-08-08T21:03:20Z'  # ede3
  by: agent  # ede3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ede3
  clock: 30  # ede3
  nonce: ede3  # ede3
  message: "CLAUSE (a1) IS UNFALSIFIABLE BY CONSTRUCTION -- restate it. CLAUSE (b) IS\nUNFALSIFIABLE ON THIS CORPUS -- it cannot close here.\n\nCLAUSE (a) HEADLINE IS GONE: d3's `function log()` -- the LOGARITHM reported as\nconsole.log -- does not reproduce. 0 of 1,352 findings carry a file-path module\nslot; pretix's 41 JS findings all carry real modules (console / localStorage /\nsessionStorage / fetch). Closed by WI-damir.\n\nCLAUSE (a1) AS MEASURED IS A TAUTOLOGY. \"1,310/1,310 findings lookup-confirmable\nagainst the production catalogue\" cannot fail: taint.py:1789/1793 and 2834/2838\ncopy sink_module / sink_primitive VERBATIM from the matched catalog entry. The\ncheck measures a copy, not a match. DO NOT CITE IT AS EVIDENCE. Restate the\nclause against WI-damir's real field (7 placeholder, 15 module != catalog).\nCounter-example the tautology hides: caddy's 11 NewRequest findings all read\nnet/http despite 75 httptest.NewRequest sites.\n\nCLAUSE (b): 0 registered sanitizer call sites across 222,103 taint call edges /\n7 repos; 0 barrier walks; 0 sanitized findings.\n  *** THE POSITIVE CONTROL NOW FIRES FOR THE FIRST TIME *** -- an 8-12 edge\n  fixture yields 2 sanitizer sites -> 2 barrier walks -> 2 sanitized findings.\n  So the zero is no longer \"not separable from receiver typing\" (the Aug-6\n  caveat is RESOLVED), but it IS still unfalsifiable on this corpus: ground\n  truth is that the corpus contains ZERO call sites of ANY catalogued sanitizer\n  (python `.encrypt(` = 1 total, on an uncatalogued RSA public key; go `.Seal(`\n  = 0; zero Fernet / AESGCM / AESCCM / ChaCha20Poly1305 references).\n  A null with no possible positive on the substrate is NOT MEASURED. To close,\n  this needs a repo that actually calls a catalogued sanitizer, or a non-crypto\n  sanitizer vocabulary.\n\nRECEIVER TYPING MEASURABLY ARMED THE SANITIZER HALF: `f: Fernet` as a parameter\nnow resolves (PR #246). Still emitting `external`: `f = Fernet(...)`,\n`f: Fernet = Fernet(...)`, and `Fernet(...).decrypt()`.\n\nNEW LATENT DEFECT FOUND HERE, filed for follow-up: taint.py\n_register_sanitizer_callers permits the WHOLE matched_list once ANY entry's\nqualified name matches, then registers all of them last-wins -- so a\nFernet.encrypt call can register as ChaCha20Poly1305. Not yet reproduced on\ncorpus (0 sanitizer sites), so it is latent, not live.\n\nFIRST REAL-REPO PRECISION DATAPOINT for verify-claims: adjudicated by reading\nsource, 3/18 realizable = 16.7% on a seeded-random sample -- BUT the denominator\nwas 93 of 313 violated evidence rows (pretix 161 and alertmanager 59 left\nunadjudicated, 70.3%), and weighted precision on the sampled 93 is 5.6%. Do NOT\nquote 16.7% as the precision. The dominant FP driver is named: prometheus's\nENTIRE 77-row host-secret-no-logging violation is seeded by one\n`os.Getenv(\"DEBUG\") != \"\"` at cmd/prometheus/main.go:346 whose value is compared\nand discarded. Prior datapoint was 50% (3/6) on a SYNTHETIC impl in March."  # ede3
